{
  "id": "c-kicad-task-01-ubuntu",
  "snapshot": "kicad-10.0.1",
  "instruction": "Symbol-Footprint Pin Consistency Audit\n\n/home/user/Desktop/opamps.kicad_sym contains 30 op-amp symbol definitions. /home/user/Desktop/opamps.pretty/ contains matching SOT-23-5 footprints (one per symbol). A subset of symbols have pin numbers that do not match the corresponding footprint pad numbers - the footprints are always correct, the symbols may be wrong.\n\nThe correct SOT-23-5 pin assignment (same for all parts) is:\nPad 1 = IN- (inverting input)\nPad 2 = IN+ (non-inverting input)\nPad 3 = V- (negative supply)\nPad 4 = OUT (output)\nPad 5 = V+ (positive supply)\n\n1. For each symbol, compare its pin numbers against the footprint pad numbers.\n2. Produce /home/user/Desktop/audit.csv listing every pin where the symbol pin number differs from the footprint pad number.\n3. Produce a corrected /home/user/Desktop/opamps.kicad_sym where all symbol pin numbers match the footprint pad numbers. Do not change footprints.\n\nRequirements:\n- /home/user/Desktop/audit.csv with columns: symbol_name, pin_name, symbol_pin_number, footprint_pad_number.\nOne row per mismatched pin (not per symbol).\n- /home/user/Desktop/opamps.kicad_sym: corrected library with 30 symbols; mismatch symbols fixed; correct symbols unchanged.\n\nWrite /home/user/Desktop/audit.csv and /home/user/Desktop/opamps.kicad_sym.",
  "source": "KiCad 9 Official Documentation — PCB Editor / Schematic Editor / CLI, Kester et al., *Analog Devices Linear Design Seminar Notes* (analog pin ordering best practice)",
